<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48301" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĭbĕrĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a Roman
				prænomen</i> (abbrev. Ti.); as, Ti. Sempronius
			Gracchus, Ti. Claudius Asellus, Ti. Claudius
			Nero.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>the emperor Tiberius</i> (whose full name
			is Ti. Claudius, Ti. F. Nero).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĭbĕ-rĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-rĕus</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the emperor Tiberius</i>, <i>Tiberian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 7, 11, § 55</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĭbĕrĭā-nus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Tiberius</i>, <i>Tiberian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scorta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetus S. C.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pira,</span>”
				<i>a kind of which Tiberius was particularly fond</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 15, 16, § 54</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĭbĕrēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Tiberius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 3, 3, 66</span></i>
			.</div>
